The '''2011 Football League Cup final''' was the final match of the [[2010–11 Football League Cup]], the 51st season of the [[Football League Cup]], a [[association football|football]] competition for the 92 teams in the [[Premier League]] and [[the Football League]]. The match was contested by [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] and [[Birmingham City F.C.|Birmingham City]], at [[Wembley Stadium]] in [[London]], on 27 February 2011.<ref>{{cite news |title=Carling Cup Draw Dates |url=http://www.carling.com/carlingcup/draw/ |work=Carling Cup official website |publisher=Molson Coors Brewing Company |access-date=24 January 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130720040850/http://www.carling.com/ |archive-date=20 July 2013 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Birmingham City won the game 2–1 and were guaranteed a spot in the third qualifying round of the [[2011–12 UEFA Europa League]].<ref>{{cite news |first=Kevin |last=McCarra |title=Obafemi Martins grabs glory as Birmingham beat Arsenal |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2011/feb/27/arsenal-birmingham-city-carling-cup-final |work=The Guardian|publisher=Guardian News and Media |date=27 February 2011 |access-date=28 February 2011 |location=London}}</ref> [[Mike Dean (referee)|Mike Dean]] was the referee.<ref name="referee">{{cite news|title=Officials named for Carling Cup final |url=http://www.football-league.co.uk/carlingcup/news/20110131/officials-named-for-carling-cup-final_2293330_2281129 |work=football-league.co.uk |publisher=The Football League |date=31 January 2011 |access-date=1 February 2011 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110211225301/http://www.football-league.co.uk/carlingcup/news/20110131/officials-named-for-carling-cup-final_2293330_2281129 |archive-date=11 February 2011 }}</ref>

==Background==
Arsenal held the advantage over Birmingham in the league matches between the two sides in [[2010–11 in English football|2010–11]], having beaten them 2–1 at the [[Emirates Stadium]] in October and again 3–0 at [[St Andrew's (stadium)|St Andrew's]] on [[New Year's Day]].<ref>{{cite news |first=Sam |last=Sheringham |title=Arsenal 2–1 Birmingham |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9085759.stm |work=BBC Sport|date=16 October 2010 |access-date=26 January 2011 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |first=Alistair |last=Magowan |title=Birmingham 0–3 Arsenal |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9328059.stm |work=BBC Sport|date=1 January 2011 |access-date=26 January 2011 }}</ref>

Arsenal had played in six Football League Cup finals, but had only won two, most recently in [[1993 Football League Cup final|1993]] when they beat [[Sheffield Wednesday F.C.|Sheffield Wednesday]] 2–1. Birmingham's only League Cup title came in [[1963 Football League Cup final|1963]], when they beat [[Second City derby|local rivals]] [[Aston Villa F.C.|Aston Villa]] 3–1 on aggregate after a two-legged final. They also reached the [[2001 Football League Cup final|2001 final]], which was played at the [[Millennium Stadium]] in [[Cardiff]] against [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]], but the 2011 final was Birmingham's first appearance in the final of a major competition at Wembley for nearly 55 years, their last being the [[1956 FA Cup final]].

